Track 3: The Queen's Flight Over Pelagic Trenches
- Story & Context: Local maritime lore in the Outer Hebrides still speaks of the night an entire swarm of migratory locusts was blown miles off course, settling on the iron deck of a cable-laying ship during a massive solar storm. The crew watched in silence as the insects died off into the dark water, while the ship’s hydrophones picked up an impossibly high-pitched harmonic resonance vibrating up from the ocean trench below. This final track mythologizes that moment, blending soaring symphonic brass with swirling accordion drones that simulate millions of paper-thin wings hitting the water. The song ends with a haunting choir vocal echoing over fading ocean swells: "Heavy wings hit the deep blue sky, where the drowned kings learn to fly."
